  "grammar": {
    "title": "Past simple: regular verbs",
    "explanation": "We use the past simple for finished actions in the past. Words like yesterday, last night, and this morning often come with it.\n\nFor regular verbs, add -ed to the verb: work -> worked, clean -> cleaned, cook -> cooked.\n\nWatch the spelling. Verbs ending in -e add only -d: like -> liked. Verbs ending in consonant + y change y to i: hurry -> hurried, study -> studied. Short verbs double the last letter: stop -> stopped, plan -> planned.\n\nFor negatives, use did not (didn't) + the verb: I did not sleep well. For questions, put Did at the start: Did you cook dinner?",
    "examples": [
      "I worked in an office yesterday.",
      "She cleaned the house this morning.",
      "We cooked dinner last night.",
      "He watched a film after lunch.",
      "They hurried to work in the traffic.",
      "I did not sleep well last night."
    ],
